    "summary_one_sentence": "In post-WWII 1949, renowned German author Thomas Mann and his daughter Erika journey through a devastated Germany, traversing the ideological divide between the American and Soviet sectors.",
    "summary_short": "Set against the backdrop of a ruined nation in 1949, Fatherland follows acclaimed writer Thomas Mann and his fiercely devoted daughter, Erika, on a historic road trip. Departing from US-dominated Frankfurt, they travel across shattered landscapes to reach Soviet-controlled Weimar. Along the way, their personal dynamic highlights the emotional and physical toll of exile, war, and political division. The narrative captures a pivotal moment in history as father and daughter confront the complex legacy of their homeland.",
    "summary_long": "In the aftermath of World War II, Germany stands physically fractured and politically partitioned into competing superpower spheres of influence. Renowned literary figure Thomas Mann returns from his American exile alongside his daughter Erika to undertake a profound journey across the devastated countryside. Starting their trip in Frankfurt, an area firmly under US military control, the duo navigates a landscape marked by rubble, moral uncertainty, and displacement. As they journey toward Weimar—the historic heart of German culture now situated in the Soviet occupation zone—they encounter citizens grappling with guilt, survival, and an uncertain future. Erika acts as both protector and intellectual sparring partner to her aging father, whose complex relationship with his native country infuses their travel with tension. Their journey serves as a living tapestry of a divided nation caught between the rising tensions of the early Cold War. Navigating bureaucratic checkpoints and ideological rifts, Thomas must reconcile his role as a cultural voice for a country that cast him out. Upon arriving in Weimar, the contrast between Germany's rich intellectual history and its grim post-war reality becomes starkly apparent. The film delivers an intimate, character-driven portrait of reconciliation, familial loyalty, and national identity during one of the 20th century's most precarious moments.",
    "synopsis": "Fatherland presents a poignant historical drama centered on legendary author Thomas Mann and his daughter Erika during their 1949 trek across a ruined, divided Germany. Moving from Western-occupied Frankfurt to Eastern-controlled Weimar, the narrative examines the fractured identity of a post-war society and the intimate bond of a family facing the ghost of their homeland.",
